Runtime hooks for Codex, Gemini CLI, and Antigravity now require explicit installation approval. Interactive CLI and text UI installs default to No; unattended installs require the matching `--enable-<agent>-hooks` flag, and Python API callers must pass `enable_<agent>_hooks=True`. Previously approved unchanged hook entries survive upgrades; changed entries require renewed approval. Codex still requires its native `/hooks` trust review.
